     "title": "Expose a pod with a ClusterIP service from YAML",
     "minutes": 4,
     "source": "",
     "task": "In namespace `arch-a`, create a Service named `basicsvc` of type ClusterIP that sends TCP port `8080` to port `80` of all pods labelled `type=webserver`. Then test it from a temporary pod.",
     "solution": "`kubectl expose` copies **all** pod labels into the selector, so with two labels on `webpod` it would select `type=webserver,tier=front`. That still works here, but the task asks for exactly `type=webserver`, so use `create service` and fix the selector, or write YAML:\n\n```bash\nk -n arch-a create service clusterip basicsvc --tcp=8080:80 $do > 2.2.yaml\n# change selector \"app: basicsvc\" to \"type: webserver\"\n```\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: basicsvc\n  namespace: arch-a\nspec:\n  type: ClusterIP\n  selector:\n    type: webserver\n  ports:\n  - protocol: TCP\n    port: 8080\n    targetPort: 80\n```",
     "verify": "```bash\nk -n arch-a get endpointslices -l kubernetes.io/service-name=basicsvc\nk -n arch-a run tmp --rm -it --restart=Never --image=busybox -- wget -qO- basicsvc:8080 | head -4\n```",
