     "title": "Two-container pod (sidecar logger)",
     "minutes": 4,
     "source": "",
     "task": "In namespace `arch-b`, create a pod `logpod` with two containers:\n- `web` running `nginx`, port 80\n- `logger` running `busybox:1.36` with command `sh -c 'while true; do date; sleep 10; done'`\n\nBoth must be running (READY `2/2`).",
     "solution": "```bash\nk create ns arch-b\nk -n arch-b run logpod --image=nginx --port=80 $do > 2.4.yaml\n# rename container to web, then append the second container\n```\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: logpod\n  namespace: arch-b\nspec:\n  containers:\n  - name: web\n    image: nginx\n    ports:\n    - containerPort: 80\n  - name: logger\n    image: busybox:1.36\n    command: [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"while true; do date; sleep 10; done\"]\n```",
