     "id": "7.9",
     "title": "Gateway API: Gateway + HTTPRoute",
     "minutes": 6,
     "source": "",
     "task": "Gateway API CRDs and a controller with GatewayClass `traefik` are installed. In namespace `gw-a`:\n- Deployment `webserver` (`nginx`), ClusterIP Service `webserver` on 80\n- Gateway `my-gateway` (class `traefik`, listener `http`, port `8000`, HTTP, routes only from the same namespace)\n- HTTPRoute `webserver-route` attached to `my-gateway` sending `PathPrefix /` to `webserver:80`",
     "solution": "```bash\nk create ns gw-a\nk -n gw-a create deployment webserver --image=nginx --port=80\nk -n gw-a expose deployment webserver --port=80 --target-port=80\n```\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Gateway\nmetadata:\n  name: my-gateway\n  namespace: gw-a\nspec:\n  gatewayClassName: traefik\n  listeners:\n  - name: http\n    port: 8000\n    protocol: HTTP\n    allowedRoutes:\n      namespaces:\n        from: Same\n---\napiVersion: gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: HTTPRoute\nmetadata:\n  name: webserver-route\n  namespace: gw-a\nspec:\n  parentRefs:\n  - name: my-gateway\n  rules:\n  - matches:\n    - path:\n        type: PathPrefix\n        value: /\n    backendRefs:\n    - name: webserver\n      port: 80\n```\n\nTraefik's HTTP entrypoint is 8000, which is why the listener uses that port.",
     "verify": "```bash\nk -n gw-a get gateway,httproute           # PROGRAMMED True, route Accepted\nk -n traefik port-forward deploy/traefik 8080:8000 &\nsleep 2\ncurl -s localhost:8080 | grep title; kill %1\n```",
     "hints": [
      "Gateway API needs two objects besides the Service: a Gateway that owns the listener, and an HTTPRoute that attaches to it via `parentRefs`.",
      "The Gateway uses `gatewayClassName: traefik`, a listener on port 8000 (Traefik's HTTP entrypoint) with `protocol: HTTP`, and `allowedRoutes.namespaces.from: Same`. The route's `rules` hold `matches` with a `PathPrefix` and `backendRefs` naming the Service and port."
     ],
     "explanation": "**What this trains:** The two Gateway API objects an application developer writes: a Gateway that opens a listener and an HTTPRoute that attaches to it.\n\n**Why the solution looks like this:**\n- The work is split across objects. The GatewayClass names the controller, the Gateway defines where traffic enters, and the HTTPRoute holds the routing rules. An Ingress puts all of that in one object.\n- `gatewayClassName: traefik` hands the Gateway to the installed controller. The listener uses port 8000 because that is Traefik's HTTP entrypoint.\n- `allowedRoutes.namespaces.from: Same` lets only routes from `gw-a` attach.\n- The HTTPRoute joins the Gateway through `parentRefs` and sends traffic to the Service through `backendRefs`. A wrong Gateway name there leaves the route unattached.\n- The status columns are the first check: the Gateway shows `PROGRAMMED True` and the route is accepted. The port-forward to Traefik then tests the path without an external address.\n\n**On the exam:** There is no generator, so copy both manifests from the kubernetes.io Gateway API page and fill gaps with `k explain gateway.spec.listeners`. The project's own site, gateway-api.sigs.k8s.io, is not allowed.\n\n**Docs:**\n- [Gateway API](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/gateway/#api-kind-gateway): Gateway and HTTPRoute examples to copy. Search: `gateway api`",
     "competencies": [
      {
       "slug": "gateway-api",
       "domain": "extras"
      }
     ]
