     "points": 5,
     "source": "Design & Build",
     "task": "Namespace `mock-2`. Create a Job `pi` that runs `perl:5.40` with command `perl -Mbignum=bpi -wle 'print bpi(200)'`. It must complete **4** times with **2** pods in parallel, retry at most **3** times, and be deleted automatically **120 s** after it finishes. Write the output of one of its pods to `/opt/course/exam/2/pi.txt`.",
     "solution": "```bash\nk -n mock-2 create job pi --image=perl:5.40 $do -- perl -Mbignum=bpi -wle 'print bpi(200)' > t2.yaml\n```\n```yaml\napiVersion: batch/v1\nkind: Job\nmetadata:\n  name: pi\n  namespace: mock-2\nspec:\n  completions: 4\n  parallelism: 2\n  backoffLimit: 3\n  ttlSecondsAfterFinished: 120\n  template:\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: pi\n        image: perl:5.40\n        command: [\"perl\", \"-Mbignum=bpi\", \"-wle\", \"print bpi(200)\"]\n      restartPolicy: Never\n```\n```bash\nmkdir -p /opt/course/exam/2\nk -n mock-2 wait --for=condition=complete job/pi --timeout=180s\nk -n mock-2 logs job/pi > /opt/course/exam/2/pi.txt     # logs from one of the job's pods\n```\nWatch out: with `ttlSecondsAfterFinished: 120` the Job and its pods disappear 2 minutes after completion, so grab the logs first.",
